                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "236491880",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198084407469",
                            "num_reviews": 253,
                            "playtime_forever": 233,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 233,
                            "last_played": 1790705817
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is a mixed review.\n\nOn one hand, I have to agree with some of the older negative reviews, especially about the absurd speed of enemy bullets compared to the ship. No matter how difficult, other Bullet Hell shmups I played felt more manageable than this. Other reviews talk of the game's development ongoing among the pages of a popular forum dedicated to the genre, but it seems to have ultimately resulted in a title tailored only to \"maniac\" players; reportedly, the bullet speed was lower during development, which is quite a bit damning.\n\nOn the other hand, there's something actually enjoyable underneath, even if it's been added only long after the original release: the 2024 Zen Mode, which uses adaptive difficulty and therefore, a lot of the time, offers much slower bullets, thus creating a more manageable challenge. It's also commendable that the developers keep maintaining the game, with the latest update in May 2026.\n\nAside from that mode, what is left is certainly a passion project, but one that seems to have taken the worst lessons from the [b]DoDonPachi[/b] model. The pixel art is also a mixed bag, ranging from some decent ships to others that look quite silly.",
